      "isPinned": false,
      "type": "video",
      "content": "This expression means “What are you doing?” but depending on the situation and tone of voice, it can also express surprise, confusion, or annoyance.\n\n📝 Let’s break it down!\n\n🔹 뭐 [mwo] = what\n🔹 하다 [hada] = to do\n🔹 는 거야 [neun geoya] = adds a sense of asking for an explanation or emphasizing curiosity about a situation\n\n💬 뭐 하는 거야? = What are you doing?\n\nYou can also say 뭐 하는 거예요? to sound more polite.\n\n💡 뭐 해? vs. 뭐 하는 거야?\n\n• 뭐 해? → What are you doing? (a simple, neutral question)\n• 뭐 하는 거야? → What are you doing? (often more emotional or emphatic)\n\nSave this reel and practice saying the expression out loud! 🐰",
      "videoUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/rjDE1WRPKP0",
      "videoTitle": "Have you ever heard someone say “뭐 하는 거야?” in a K-drama? 🇰🇷",
